      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "District 3 is the most likely initial hotspot due to its high density and low-income population, which correlates with poorer living conditions and limited access to healthcare. District 2 is also a significant risk because of its high density and reliance on public transit, which facilitates rapid transmission. Districts 1 and 4, with their higher incomes and better access to care, are less likely to see explosive initial outbreaks.",
